WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:03.236
Albert was a shining god
of comedy.

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.671
He was speaking directly to me.
(LAUGHS)

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.740
Always something just different.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:08.908
He was like a comedic tornado.

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:13.212
Just fearless and funny.
He's so fuckin' hot.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.715
It took this
to finally hear a compliment.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:17.650
-(LAUGHS)
-Can't wait till I'm dead.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.285
ROB REINER:
<i> So, here's the thing.</i>

00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:21.754
We've been friends for, like,
almost 60 years.

00:00:22.187 --> 00:00:23.823
I've always looked up to you

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:25.592
and what you could do
with comedy.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:29.528
I did 100 variety shows.

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:30.329
Albert Brooks!

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.832
-Albert Brooks.
-Albert Brooks.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:33.999
Albert Brooks.

00:00:34.099 --> 00:00:37.503
This... This isn't me.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.671
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.039
You're the only guy I know

00:00:40.105 --> 00:00:41.507
who would go
on national television

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.510
<i> with a routine
that you had never tried out.</i>

00:00:44.576 --> 00:00:46.245
ALBERT BROOKS:
<i> I went in the bathroom,</i>

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.014
<i>I would come up with something,</i>

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.315
and I would go do it.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.784
Not only don't you have
any money,

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:53.553
but your sister is dead!

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.221
That was funny.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.455
♪ (UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING) ♪

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:59.559
He was the first
alternative comic.

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:01.827
I think of him
as the caviar of comedy.

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:03.730
This guy's really special.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:08.768 line:0%
CHRIS ROCK:<i> He's so good,
 you can't steal it.</i>

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.136
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.237
If you stole it,

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:12.639
you wouldn't know
what to do with it.

00:01:13.405 --> 00:01:15.775 line:0%
I mean, he's a beautiful actor.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.244 line:0%
He has all that technique.
He can do anything.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.213 line:0%
And I'm in love with you.

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:22.749
How do you like that?

00:01:23.849 --> 00:01:25.418
I buried the lede.

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:29.389 line:0%
ALBERT:
<i>Stanley Kubrick called me
 and said,</i>

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:32.224 line:0%
"This is the jealousy movie
I've always wanted to make."

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:34.327
You've heard of
a no-win situation, haven't you?

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:35.628
-Vietnam, this.
-No.

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:38.031
I'm telling you, they're around.
I think we're in one of them.

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:41.867 line:0%
Everything he was talking about
is what television turned into.

00:01:41.967 --> 00:01:43.703
Film the gynecologist?

00:01:44.903 --> 00:01:45.938
What you didn't want to happen

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:47.340 line:0%
watching
an Albert Brook's movie,

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.942 line:0%
<i>you never wanted the scenes
 to ever end.</i>

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:53.880
<i>Defending Your Life</i> was one
of the most insightful films

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:54.914
I had ever seen.

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:57.116
-Hi. How'd you die?
-On stage, like you.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.317
(LAUGHTER)

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:00.887
To me,
genius is you have the idea

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.788
<i> and then the courage
 to execute it.</i>

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:04.256
(LAUGHTER)

00:02:04.356 --> 00:02:06.926
I would rather have
Albert's career than my career.

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:08.527
ROB:<i> I mean,
I'm listening to all this,</i>

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.130
and I'm getting a person
who's been defending his life.

00:02:11.196 --> 00:02:13.032
Every goddamn minute.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.066
ROB:<i> Yeah.</i>

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:15.134
ALBERT:<i> My agent said,</i>

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:18.003
<i> "I don't know why
you always take the hard road."</i>

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:20.273
-(SCREAMS)
-You think I see two roads.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.542
-Yeah.
-I see one road!

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:26.712
Because this... (SCOFFS)
this isn't me.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:27.747
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:29.349
It's not the real me.

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:32.985
♪ (PIANO MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:34.086
This...

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:36.222
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.656
...is the real me.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.092
He's the funniest man
in the world.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:44.831 line:0%
(APPLAUSE)

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.466
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

